# Local instructions (private: gitignored, never commit)

## Internal planning docs

Internal planning material is cloned at `.internal/` inside this repo.

- Design and plan documents: `.internal/docs/`

Before starting a task, read the relevant internal docs. Work through the plan in order and flag any deviation before making it.

## Rules for private material

- Never copy or closely paraphrase content from `.internal/` into any tracked file: code, comments, docs, README, test fixtures, commit messages, PR or issue text, or `CLAUDE.md`.
- Write public code and docs in generic technical terms.
- `.internal/` is its own git repository. Commit changes to it from inside `.internal/` (`git -C .internal ...`). Never `git add .internal` and never use `git add -f`.
- Review `git diff --cached` for leaked private details before every commit or push.
